// XFAIL: RT-C301-10: an i32 computed from untyped literals reaches an i64 use through a form the check does not follow (a match on `Some(a + a)`, its binding the use's): widened after the i32 arithmetic (0.30.2)
// From review 4 (w04): match Some(a + a) { Some(v) => println("{}", take(v)), None => {} }
// rustc types the literals i64 and prints 4000000000; vole computes a + a in i32, gets -294967296 at -O0 and -O2 (no overflow panic: the sum of two constants is folded), and take's contract stops it (take.neg).
// EXPECT: 4000000000
fn take(x: i64) -> i64 requires x > 0 else "take.neg: {x}" { x }

fn main() {
    let a = 2000000000;
    match Some(a + a) {
        Some(v) => println("{}", take(v)),
        None => {}
    }
}
